Semantics, read them twice:
- fitting_math: strictly mode-gated. Only the Marp engine wraps formulas with `data-marp-fitting-math` in slide mode; the third-party math rules are explicitly disabled there to prevent double-rendering, so plain-markdown math never produces this marker.
- hljs vs base_highlight: mutually exclusive per render. Slide mode installs the marp highlighter in place of the original — recognized languages produce hljs-marked output, the base highlighter never runs. Plain markdown calls the original highlight function unchanged, which is what the `baseHighlight` marker detects. Unrecognized language in slide mode returns an empty string and markdown-it falls back to default rendering with the `language-<lang>` class — no hljs marker.
- The mermaid case in slide mode goes through the highlighter's mermaid branch (`<div class="mermaid">`), not hljs, not base.

That is the full highlighter precedence story. Three points delivered — build against these before you come back asking for mermaid and unknown_lang files.

